{
  "id": "Compound::DB01078 - Gene::478",
  "verbalization": "Deslanoside appears to interact with Atp1a3 through a series of molecular pathways involving Fxyd2 and glycoside-based compounds. The evidence suggests that Deslanoside binds to Fxyd2, which then participates in sodium-potassium-exchanging Atpase activity, ultimately leading to the activation of Atp1a3. This pathway is supported by the lowest common ancestor analysis, which links Deslanoside and Acetyldigitoxin to the glycoside class, and further to the Cardenolide Glycoside, a known inhibitor of Atp1a3. The shared interaction with Fxyd2 and the involvement of Atp1a3 in potassium transport highlight a potential mechanism by which Deslanoside may modulate Atp1a3 activity. The evidence from multiple paths supports a direct or indirect relationship through Fxyd2, suggesting that Deslanoside may influence Atp1a3 through a glycoside-mediated mechanism, possibly by modulating ion transport activity.",
